==Post-match==
As President of [[The Football Association]], [[Prince William, Duke of Cambridge]] would normally have attended the final and presented the trophy to the winning captain at the conclusion of the game. However, as the final was scheduled for the same day as his [[Wedding of Prince Harry and Meghan Markle|brother's wedding]], for which he was serving as [[best man]],<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.itv.com/news/2018-03-27/prince-william-will-miss-the-fa-cup-final-to-attend-harry-and-meghans-wedding/ |title=Prince William will miss the FA Cup final to attend Harry and Meghan's wedding |last=Ship |first=Chris |date=27 March 2018 |publisher=[[ITV News]] |access-date=27 April 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180428093658/http://www.itv.com/news/2018-03-27/prince-william-will-miss-the-fa-cup-final-to-attend-harry-and-meghans-wedding/ |archive-date=28 April 2018 |url-status=live }}</ref> the trophy was instead presented by Jackie Wilkins, the widow of former Manchester United and Chelsea player Ray Wilkins, who died in April 2018.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44127712 |title=FA Cup final: Ray Wilkins' widow to present trophy to winners |date=15 May 2018 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |access-date=15 May 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180520012342/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44127712 |archive-date=20 May 2018 |url-status=live }}</ref> Chelsea's Rüdiger was named [[Player of the match|man of the match]].<ref name="report"/>

Cahill, the winning captain, said "We had a lot of defending to do{{nbsp}}... This is a dream come true, as this is the first one as captain".<ref name=guardlive2/> Hazard added: "We tried to defend well. We scored one goal, it's enough today."<ref name=guardlive2/> Conte was upbeat: "I'm very satisfied because today was very difficult{{nbsp}}... It showed great desire to finish the season in the right way despite the great difficulty we have had".<ref name=summary/> Mourinho was indignant in defeat: "I congratulate them because they won, but I don't think they deserve to win. I congratulate because I am a sportsman."<ref name=guardlive2/> He also opined: "Every defeat hurts, but for me personally the ones that hurt less are when you give everything and you go without any regrets".<ref name=summary/> [[BBC Sport]] correspondent [[Phil McNulty]] highlighted the performance of the Chelsea players Hazard, Courtois, Kanté, Cahill and Rüdiger, while criticising United trio Jones, Sánchez and Pogba.<ref name=summary/> Sam Wallace, writing in ''[[The Daily Telegraph]]'' declared that "this was a dreadful final".<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2018/05/19/fa-cup-final-2018-chelsea-vs-manchester-united-live-score-updates/ |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=10 July 2020 |date=20 May 2018 |first1=Sam |last1=Wallace |first2=JJ |last2=Bull |title=Eden Hazard penalty settles FA Cup final as Chelsea edge past Man Utd |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190902214330/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2018/05/19/fa-cup-final-2018-chelsea-vs-manchester-united-live-score-updates/ |archive-date=2 September 2019 |url-status=live |url-access=subscription }}</ref>

Chelsea won £1.8{{nbsp}}million for winning the final and became the first club to win the FA Cup, the [[Women's FA Cup]] and the [[FA Youth Cup]] in the same season.<ref name="report"/> As winners, Chelsea qualified for the group stage of the [[2018–19 UEFA Europa League]], although they had qualified for that phase already via their league position.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/43402150 |title=Premier League and Football League: Ups & downs and European qualification |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=29 April 2018 |access-date=1 May 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180430063029/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/43402150 |archive-date=30 April 2018 |url-status=live }}</ref> This meant that Arsenal, who finished sixth in the league, gained qualification for the Europa League.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44016356 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 12 October 2020 | title = European qualification: Premier League sides set to discover their fate | date = 6 May 2018 | archive-date = 12 October 2020 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20201012150126/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44016356 | url-status = live }}</ref> Chelsea also earned the right to play 2017–18 Premier League champions [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] for the [[2018 FA Community Shield]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44995783 |title=Chelsea 0–2 Manchester City |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |access-date=10 July 2020 |date=5 August 2018 |first=Chris |last=Bevan |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190402174434/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44995783 |archive-date=2 April 2019 |url-status=live }}</ref>

It was the first time that Mourinho had lost a cup final in charge of an English team, after seven consecutive victories,<ref name=summary/> and the defeat sealed his third-ever full season without winning silverware.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/fa-cup-final-chelsea-manchester-united-penalty-fires-to-victory-a8359726.html |work=[[The Independent]] |access-date=10 July 2020 |date=19 May 2018 |title=Eden Hazard penalty fires Chelsea to victory against Manchester United in flat FA Cup final |first=Miguel |last=Delaney |archive-date=16 June 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190616113244/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/fa-cup-final-chelsea-manchester-united-penalty-fires-to-victory-a8359726.html |url-status=live }}</ref> It was the first domestic cup won by Conte, who lost the [[2012 Coppa Italia Final]] with [[Juventus FC|Juventus]] and the previous season's FA Cup Final as Chelsea manager.<ref name=summary/> Conte was sacked by Chelsea in July 2018 before becoming the manager of [[Inter Milan]] on a three-year deal beginning with the [[2019–20 Serie A]] season.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44820563 | title = Antonio Conte: Chelsea sack Italian after two years in charge | date = 13 July 2018 | access-date = 10 October 2020 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | archive-date = 18 August 2020 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20200818174451/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44820563 | url-status = live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2019/05/31/antonio-conte-named-new-inter-milan-manager/ |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=31 May 2019 |access-date=10 July 2020 |title=Antonio Conte named new Inter Milan manager |agency=[[Press Association]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190531134247/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2019/05/31/antonio-conte-named-new-inter-milan-manager/ |archive-date=31 May 2019 |url-status=live }}</ref> He was replaced by [[Maurizio Sarri]] the following day.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44825638 |title=Maurizio Sarri: Chelsea name ex-Napoli boss as Antonio Conte's successor |date=14 July 2018 |access-date=10 July 2020 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200615220556/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/44825638 |archive-date=15 June 2020 |url-status=live }}</ref> Mourinho remained through the summer at Manchester United, but, that December, with Manchester United 19 points behind the league leaders Liverpool, he was dismissed.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/46603018 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |access-date=10 July 2020 |title=Jose Mourinho: Manchester United sack manager |first=Simon |last=Stone |date=18 December 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200616175525/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/46603018 |archive-date=16 June 2020 |url-status=live }}</ref>

